# The repair workers' slice: their builds, lints, audits, agents, git work and background
# publications yield the CPU and disk to the CI and staging VMs on the same host.
#
# The name puts it under tauceti.slice, beside TauCetiFleet's tauceti-fleet.slice, which holds the
# VMs. The cgroup CPU controller shares a busy host between siblings by weight, whatever the
# processes' nice values: in app.slice (weight 100, beside tauceti.slice at 100) the workers were
# never below the VMs, however reniced. Here the workers get roughly a tenth of what the VMs get
# when both want more CPU than tauceti.slice has, and whatever the VMs leave otherwise (the weights
# are work-conserving, so repairs are slowed, never stopped). IOWeight acts only where the block
# layer weighs cgroups (BFQ, or io.cost configured for the device); on devices using the `none`
# scheduler without io.cost, as on tauchonki2 in 2026-11, nothing here orders disk traffic.
#
# MemoryHigh is a reclaim threshold, meant to reduce how hard the repairs' memory, mostly file cache,
# presses on the staging VM. On tauchonki2 (125 GiB) the staging VM has 64 GiB and the OS keeps
# about 12 GiB, which leaves about 48 GiB, before the native PR runners (which reserve nothing);
# repairs measured 36 GiB resident with two builds at once (2026-11-19). Above it the kernel reclaims
# from the slice (file cache or, through swap, anonymous memory) and slows the slice's allocations.
# Crossing it does not itself invoke the OOM killer (there is no MemoryMax), though host-wide
# pressure still can. The repair builds' compiler wrapper ignores memory.high, so a working set above
# it (compilers plus the .olean files they map) thrashes instead of waiting. If repairs slow down,
# check the slice's memory.pressure, memory.events and swap activity, and raise the value or reduce
# repair concurrency. systemctl --user daemon-reload applies a change to the running slice.
#
# install-repair.sh installs this file; never add a drop-in for it.

[Unit]
Description=Tau Ceti queue repair workers, below CI and staging builds
Documentation=https://github.com/TauCetiProject/TauCetiWorker/blob/main/docs/queue/operations.md

[Slice]
CPUWeight=10
IOWeight=10
MemoryHigh=48G
